1
00:02:11,319 --> 00:02:12,319
Have an apple.

2
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,240
Ignore me?

3
00:02:22,139 --> 00:02:23,599
You don't have to pretend with me.

4
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:26,919
I know you're awake.

5
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:36,659
Is there nothing

6
00:02:36,659 --> 00:02:38,000
that can

7
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,860
touch you anymore?

8
00:02:49,199 --> 00:02:50,860
I forgot to tell you,

9
00:02:51,939 --> 00:02:53,759
on the day your child died,

10
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,419
I was at the hospital.

11
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,939
I could have saved him.

12
00:03:11,819 --> 00:03:12,419
What?

13
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,159
What did you say?

14
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,919
How could I possibly let him live?

15
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,259
Remind me,

16
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,120
that's your child with Yu Changxuan.

17
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:30,039
Only when this bastard is gone,

18
00:03:30,979 --> 00:03:32,400
there will be

19
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:35,199
nothing between you and me

20
00:03:35,199 --> 00:03:36,460
to hinder us.

21
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,400
Only when he's dead,

22
00:03:40,419 --> 00:03:42,599
can you truly be mine,

23
00:03:44,539 --> 00:03:46,180
completely.

24
00:03:47,159 --> 00:03:49,360
Jiang Xueting, I will kill you!

25
00:04:09,819 --> 00:04:10,819
Why?

26
00:04:11,759 --> 00:04:12,500
Pingjun,

27
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,860
dying by your hand,

28
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,379
I...

29
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,660
I'm glad.

30
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:37,079
Don't cry.

31
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,500
Your child

32
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:46,579
is alive.

33
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,720
What are you saying?

34
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:52,779
Ziyi said

35
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,680
Xie Zao Hua

36
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:00,040
took your child

37
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,560
from the hospital

38
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,839
to Nanhua.

39
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,100
Why did you...

40
00:05:16,339 --> 00:05:17,759
Why did you say that?

41
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:38,079
I bombed the factory of Fujiwara.

42
00:05:38,699 --> 00:05:40,519
Many Japanese died.

43
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,839
They won't let me go.

44
00:05:44,279 --> 00:05:45,420
I've done

45
00:05:47,459 --> 00:05:49,459
too many wrong things in my life.

46
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,759
I'm most sorry for you.

47
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,399
In the end,

48
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,720
I just want to

49
00:06:01,019 --> 00:06:02,420
die in your hands.

50
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,839
This is the pass.

51
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,040
Take it.

52
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,740
Leave the city

53
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:27,339
and find him.

54
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,399
Hurry up.

55
00:06:33,199 --> 00:06:34,740
There's no time left.

56
00:06:39,819 --> 00:06:40,860
Let's go.

57
00:06:42,459 --> 00:06:43,620
Go.

58
00:06:54,379 --> 00:06:55,279
[Pingjun,]

59
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,459
[you're finally]

60
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,180
[free.]

61
00:07:11,879 --> 00:07:12,699
[Xueting,]

62
00:07:13,459 --> 00:07:14,980
[I was shocked to read]

63
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,379
[your letter today.]

64
00:07:16,819 --> 00:07:17,899
[You're studying abroad,]

65
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,279
[seeking knowledge to help]

66
00:07:19,279 --> 00:07:20,759
[China rise.]

67
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:21,860
[I'm also working hard]

68
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,579
[at school.]

69
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,500
[Today, our teacher said,]

70
00:07:25,899 --> 00:07:27,920
[a strong youth makes a strong nation.]

71
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,860
[and I thought of you.]

72
00:07:30,699 --> 00:07:31,740
[I believe]

73
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,279
[you will become]

74
00:07:33,279 --> 00:07:34,740
[the backbone of this turbulent world.]

75
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,519
[People say that plum blossoms are the most resilient,]

76
00:07:38,199 --> 00:07:40,240
[so I embroidered a handkerchief with a plum blossom.]

77
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,300
[I hope you return soon]

78
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:43,800
[and achieve great things.]

79
00:07:45,379 --> 00:07:46,120
[Xueting,]

80
00:07:46,579 --> 00:07:47,600
[everything is fine at home.]

81
00:07:48,339 --> 00:07:49,639
[Mother made]

82
00:07:49,639 --> 00:07:51,620
[your favorite osmanthus cake yesterday,]

83
00:07:52,259 --> 00:07:53,959
[waiting for you to come back and try it.]

84
00:07:54,779 --> 00:07:56,040
[I have some good news.]

85
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,040
[The modern play I wrote,]

86
00:07:58,199 --> 00:07:59,300
[A New Life of Nora,]

87
00:07:59,399 --> 00:08:00,699
[has been staged at the girls' school.]

88
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:03,480
[The teacher praised my work.]

89
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,399
[I want more people to know]

90
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:07,500
[that both men and women]

91
00:08:07,939 --> 00:08:08,600
[can take control]

92
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,920
[of their own destiny.]

93
00:08:11,779 --> 00:08:12,800
[I look forward to your return.]

94
00:09:20,259 --> 00:09:20,740
Mr. Yu,

95
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,860
the Jiang's Mansion is just ahead.

96
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:35,919
Next one.

97
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:55,899
Brother Wu,

98
00:09:56,539 --> 00:09:58,139
We've searched the whole city,

99
00:09:58,539 --> 00:09:59,940
but still no sign of her.

100
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,580
By the time you read this letter,

101
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,620
I will have already left Nanhuai.

102
00:10:31,019 --> 00:10:32,779
All these days I've spent by your side,

103
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:34,179
it's not that I haven't thought about it—

104
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,279
perhaps one day,

105
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,740
I could take Ye Pingjun's place

106
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,059
in your heart.

107
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:40,919
But the longer time goes on,

108
00:10:41,039 --> 00:10:42,279
the more clearly I see—

109
00:10:43,179 --> 00:10:44,799
your heart has always belonged only to her.

110
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,019
No one else can squeeze in.

111
00:10:48,779 --> 00:10:50,200
I'm not leaving because I'm heartbroken.

112
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,240
but I suddenly felt

113
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,519
that the world was in turmoil,

114
00:10:54,919 --> 00:10:56,279
and many people were suffering,

115
00:10:56,679 --> 00:10:58,379
and many people were homeless.

116
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,059
If I still

117
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:01,720
pursued an unrequited love,

118
00:11:02,519 --> 00:11:03,179
I would

119
00:11:03,179 --> 00:11:04,059
look down upon myself.

120
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,379
I always thought

121
00:11:06,639 --> 00:11:07,740
that people

122
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:09,019
should live for something.

123
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:10,740
I used to think

124
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:11,820
that "something" was you.

125
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,639
[Now I want to try]

126
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,299
[if I can do something]

127
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:16,100
[for more people.]

128
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:17,960
[The more turbulent the world,]

129
00:11:18,259 --> 00:11:20,059
[the more we need to do something.]

130
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:22,340
[Maybe I can't do much,]

131
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,299
[but it's better than being stuck here.]

132
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,720
[I believe]

133
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,399
[you will support me.]

134
00:11:29,639 --> 00:11:30,720
[Take care of yourself]

135
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,320
[no matter where you are.]

136
00:12:09,179 --> 00:12:10,799
[Newspapers!]

137
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,419
[Newspapers!]

138
00:12:13,559 --> 00:12:15,159
[Japanese troops are increasing in Manchuria,]

139
00:12:15,159 --> 00:12:17,740
[and the situation outside the pass is on the verge of explosion.]

140
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,019
You want this?

141
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:39,500
Here.

142
00:12:40,799 --> 00:12:41,759
The bigger one is for you.

143
00:12:42,539 --> 00:12:43,240
Go.

144
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,639
Thank you, miss.

145
00:12:53,379 --> 00:12:55,519
I have a child too.

146
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,279
Once we cross this ridge,

147
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:06,379
we're not far from Nanjing.

148
00:13:07,139 --> 00:13:08,000
Yeah.

149
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:10,679
We're heading south

150
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,919
just to survive.

151
00:13:14,039 --> 00:13:14,740
Girl,

152
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,080
I've noticed you've been

153
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,000
traveling alone.

154
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,799
Are you heading to Nanjing to find relatives,

155
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,019
or Shanghai?

156
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:25,059
I'm going to Nanhuai.

157
00:13:25,559 --> 00:13:27,840
What? Nanhuai?

158
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,019
Girl,

159
00:13:30,299 --> 00:13:31,700
are you out of your mind?

160
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,759
Everyone's fleeing south.

161
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,960
Nanhuai is a major city,

162
00:13:36,019 --> 00:13:37,159
not far from

163
00:13:37,159 --> 00:13:38,100
the Japanese.

164
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,919
You're going back north?

165
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,019
Yeah, girl,

166
00:13:41,019 --> 00:13:42,700
heading north now

167
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,519
is like walking into a trap.

168
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,740
Yeah.

169
00:13:45,879 --> 00:13:47,659
Why are you heading north?

170
00:13:48,519 --> 00:13:50,519
My husband and child

171
00:13:52,279 --> 00:13:54,000
are all there.

172
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:01,080
If I can't

173
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:03,000
get back to them,

174
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,480
wherever I go,

175
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,620
I'll be a wanderer.

176
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:58,899
Don't cry.

177
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:00,419
Don't cry.

178
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,259
Don't cry.

179
00:15:13,899 --> 00:15:15,039
Don't cry.

180
00:15:22,299 --> 00:15:23,139
Charge!

181
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:25,039
One, two, one.

182
00:15:25,039 --> 00:15:25,779
Charge!

183
00:15:25,779 --> 00:15:27,159
Defend our country!

184
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:28,000
Defend our country!

185
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:28,879
Hurry up!

186
00:15:28,879 --> 00:15:29,659
Charge!

187
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,000
One, two, one!

188
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,600
Keep up!

189
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,220
Charge!

190
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:33,440
Run!

191
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,820
Defend our country!

192
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:35,700
Charge!

193
00:15:36,179 --> 00:15:36,860
Brother.

194
00:15:37,419 --> 00:15:38,259
Urgent message from the border.

195
00:15:39,179 --> 00:15:40,320
In the past month,

196
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,480
the Japanese military

197
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,919
has been conducting more frequent exercises

198
00:15:42,919 --> 00:15:43,620
along the South Manchurian Railway.

199
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,840
They used to only train during the day,

200
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:47,340
but now they continue even at night,

201
00:15:47,779 --> 00:15:48,899
and have even intruded into

202
00:15:48,899 --> 00:15:50,500
the alert area without prior notice.

203
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,240
Before a wolf kills,

204
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,399
it sharpens its teeth.

205
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,019
Pass my order.

206
00:15:56,419 --> 00:15:57,320
All levels of defense areas

207
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:59,159
should be on first-degree alert.

208
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:00,220
Kill.

209
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:00,679
Yes.

210
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:03,059
Kill.

211
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,320
The people we sent out,

212
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,519
around Jiangcheng,

213
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:09,740
and at all the checkpoints,

214
00:16:10,779 --> 00:16:11,820
none of them found Sister-in-law.

215
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:19,220
We've been searching for so long,

216
00:16:19,419 --> 00:16:20,440
not a single trace.

217
00:16:21,779 --> 00:16:22,960
I'm just saying, hypothetically,

218
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,279
could she already be...

219
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:24,879
No.

220
00:16:27,259 --> 00:16:28,000
I have a feeling.

221
00:16:30,919 --> 00:16:32,019
Pingjun is not dead.

222
00:16:33,779 --> 00:16:35,059
She must still be alive.

223
00:16:35,799 --> 00:16:37,379
Yes, I also think so.

224
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:38,700
But what if...

225
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,700
There's no what if.

226
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,299
If I can't find her in a day,

227
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:42,700
I'll keep looking for a day.

228
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:44,460
If I can't find her in a year,

229
00:16:45,559 --> 00:16:46,659
I'll keep looking for a year.

230
00:16:47,399 --> 00:16:48,100
Five years.

231
00:16:48,919 --> 00:16:49,639
Ten years.

232
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:51,639
Twenty years.

233
00:16:53,399 --> 00:16:54,500
As long as I, Yu Changxuan,

234
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,779
still have a breath in me,

235
00:16:57,159 --> 00:16:58,740
I will keep searching.

236
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,820
Go!

237
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,200
Zening, come and play with me.

238
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:24,799
Mom,

239
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:25,779
Qixuan said

240
00:17:25,779 --> 00:17:27,000
she had safely arrived

241
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,720
at the war hospital in the suburbs of Beicheng

242
00:17:29,059 --> 00:17:30,240
and was working as a nurse there.

243
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,220
She said everything was settled,

244
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,500
and we shouldn't worry about her.

245
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,039
This child

246
00:17:36,539 --> 00:17:38,000
left a letter

247
00:17:38,339 --> 00:17:39,500
and ran away from home

248
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,259
to find that Xiao Beichen.

249
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,220
She's so stubborn

250
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:44,859
that no one can change her mind.

251
00:17:45,359 --> 00:17:46,140
Mom,

252
00:17:46,339 --> 00:17:47,200
you know

253
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,420
her best.

254
00:17:48,619 --> 00:17:49,960
Her room

255
00:17:50,059 --> 00:17:52,500
is full of

256
00:17:52,619 --> 00:17:53,380
clippings

257
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:54,599
of Xiao Beichen.

258
00:17:55,039 --> 00:17:56,099
She's been

259
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:57,819
obsessed with him for a long time.

260
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:00,960
Field hospitals in the rear

261
00:18:01,279 --> 00:18:03,119
are relatively safe.

262
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,319
She's happy to do

263
00:18:07,539 --> 00:18:09,819
what she wants to do.

264
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,059
As long as it's her wish,

265
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:15,099
I will support her,

266
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:17,000
no matter how far it is.

267
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:20,279
I'll wait for her at home.

268
00:18:21,059 --> 00:18:23,059
As long as she is safe,

269
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,859
I don't care when she comes back.

270
00:18:28,819 --> 00:18:29,940
You are back.

271
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:33,319
Daddy hugs you.

272
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,240
Little boy.

273
00:18:35,859 --> 00:18:36,519
Why are you

274
00:18:36,519 --> 00:18:38,059
coming back so late today?

275
00:18:38,059 --> 00:18:38,740
Yeah.

276
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:40,000
Have a rest.

277
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,019
Uncle, did you bring me

278
00:18:41,019 --> 00:18:42,539
something to eat?

279
00:18:43,799 --> 00:18:44,559
Thank you, uncle.

280
00:18:44,559 --> 00:18:45,180
You're welcome.

281
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,640
Share it with everyone.

282
00:18:48,119 --> 00:18:49,559
Was Xiaoyu well-behaved today?

283
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,440
Yes.

284
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,460
Xiaoyu listened

285
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,779
to grandma and aunt.

286
00:18:53,779 --> 00:18:54,559
Really?

287
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,000
He has been waiting for you

288
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
all day.

289
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,259
I want dad to hold me.

290
00:19:12,759 --> 00:19:14,599
Dad, I want to hear a story.

291
00:19:15,259 --> 00:19:16,339
I'll continue to tell you

292
00:19:16,339 --> 00:19:17,019
Peter Pan.

293
00:19:20,859 --> 00:19:22,880
Wendy and her brothers

294
00:19:23,119 --> 00:19:24,400
all flew away

295
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,319
with Peter Pan.

296
